warning[SCXML077]: `<script>` changes the system variable `_event`
 --> tests/ui/scxml077-system-variable-writes.scxml:6:22
  |
6 |       <script>delete _event; _name += '!';</script>
  |                      ^^^^^^ `_event` is a read-only system variable
  |
  = note: SCXML 1.0 §5.10: "The Processor MUST cause any attempt to change the value of a system variable to fail and MUST place the error 'error.execution' on the internal event queue when such an attempt is made." The change fails at run time with `error.execution`; a non-strict `delete` or a reflective deletion through the global object returns `false` without one (a known limitation, docs/spec-errata.md). Variable names beginning with '_' are reserved for system use, and '_x' is the root of platform-specific system variables.
  = help: copy `_event` into a `<data>` variable and change that copy, or use a name that does not begin with `_`
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §5.10 System Variables
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model

